findings.body:
Removing `@require_role("admin")` leaves `DELETE /users/<user>` with no authentication or authorization. Any client that can reach the app can delete arbitrary accounts via `USERS.remove(user)` and receive `204`.

Cleanup jobs running as `viewer` need a deliberate grant (service role, scoped job token, or separate internal endpoint with its own auth), not an open delete. Restore a caller-identity check before merge; the current `require_role` also keys off the path `user` rather than the caller, so replace it with a real principal check rather than dropping the guard.

```suggestion
@require_role("admin")
def delete_user(user):
```
